-11-01","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"opendoar____::eda80a3d5b344bc40f3bc04f65b7a357","value":"PubMed Central"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::eda80a3d5b344bc40f3bc04f65b7a357","value":"PubMed Central"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"3208409862"},{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.18632/aging.203663"}],"type":"Other literature type","urls":["https://dx.doi.org/10.18632/aging.203663"],"refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::5f532a3fc4f1ea403f37070f59a7a53a","value":"Microsoft Academic Graph"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"3208409862"},{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.18632/aging.203663"}],"type":"Other literature type","urls":["https://dx.doi.org/10.18632/aging.203663"],"refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::5f532a3fc4f1ea403f37070f59a7a53a","value":"Microsoft Academic Graph"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":true,"isGreen":true,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Ahmed El-Abd Ahmed","name":"Ahmed El-Abd","surname":"Ahmed","rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid_pending","value":"0000-0002-1843-5411"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Sawsan M.A. Abuhamdah","name":"Sawsan M.A.","surname":"Abuhamdah","rank":2,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid_pending","value":"0000-0001-5886-5742"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Mohammed H. Hassan","name":"Mohammed H.","surname":"Hassan","rank":3,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid_pending","value":"0000-0003-2698-9438"},"provenance":null}},{"id":"orcid_______::7330386b20c2fee653ead867784c85f7","fullName":"Nagwan I. Rashwan","name":"Nagwan I.","surname":"Rashwan","rank":4,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-7497-0398"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Eman A. Abd-Elmawgood","name":"Eman A.","surname":"Abd-Elmawgood","rank":5,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid_pending","value":"0000-0003-0006-0487"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Haggagy Mansour","name":"Haggagy","surname":"Mansour","rank":6,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid_pending","value":"0000-0001-8740-6131"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Hoda S. Sherkawy","name":"Hoda S.","surname":"Sherkawy","rank":7,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Shymaa G. Rizk","name":"Shymaa G.","surname":"Rizk","rank":8,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":"gold","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0303 health sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"03 medical and health sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"pediatric multisystem inflammatory disease"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"covid-19 related; tumor necrosis factor-alpha converting enzyme; tumor necrosis factor-alpha; angiotensin converting enzyme; single nucleotide polymorphisms"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Original Article"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Pediatrics"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"RJ1-570"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Clinical, biochemical, and genetic study of TACE/TNF-α/ACE signaling pathway in pediatric COVID-19 infection","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p>Background: Pediatric patients infected with coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) have unique clinical characteristics. Tumor necrosis factor (TNF) is a proinflammatory cytokine that greatly contributes to tumor pathogenesis.Purpose: To describe the presenting characteristics of COVID-19 infection among pediatric patients, and investigate the possible role of the TNF-α signaling pathway.Methods: This prospective case-control study included 50 Egyptian pediatric patients with COVID-19 and 50 healthy controls. Clinical, laboratory, and radiological assessments were performed. Serum TNF-alpha (TNF-α), TNF-α-converting enzyme (TACE), and angiotensin-converting enzyme 2 (ACE2) were measured using enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay. ACE (I/D) (rs4646994), ACE2 rs2285666, and TNF-α-308G/A single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) were performed using conventional polymerase chain reaction techniques with or without restriction fragment length polymorphism.Results: The median age was 1 year (interquartile range [IQR], 0.31–2.50 years) in the case group and 1.45 years (IQR, 1.00–3.00) in the control group. The main presenting symptoms were fever (92%), dry cough (74%), and dyspnea (72%). The lymphocytic count was normal in 14 patients (28%), decreased in 16 patients (32%), and increased in 20 patients (40%) of the case group. Positive chest computed tomography finding of COVID-19 infection were demonstrated among 40% of patients using COVID-19 Reporting and Data System categories (ground-glass opacity with or without consolidations in the lungs). There were significant increased serum TACE and TNF-α with decreased ACE2 levels among cases versus controls (P&lt; 0.001). The GG genotype and G allele of the TNF-α-308G/A SNP were significantly higher in patients than in controls (P&lt;0.05 for both), with insignificant differences in genotype and allelic frequencies in the ACE (I/D) (rs4646994) and ACE2 rs2285666 SNPs.Conclusion: The TNF signaling pathway was significantly activated in pediatric COVID-19 infection. Only the TNF-α-308G/A SNP was significantly associated with pediatric COVID-19 infection.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2024-12-15","publisher":"Korean Pediatric Society","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref","Clin Exp Pediatr","Clinical and Experimental Pediatrics, Vol 67, Iss 12, Pp 704-717 (2024)"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code"